.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
QHBoxLayout \- Lines up widgets horizontally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
\fC#include <qlayout.h>\fR
.PP
Inherits QBoxLayout.
.PP
.SS "Public Members"
.in +1c
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQHBoxLayout\fR ( QWidget * " "parent" ", int " "border" "=0, int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 )"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQHBoxLayout\fR ( QLayout * " "parentLayout" ", int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 )"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQHBoxLayout\fR ( int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 )"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fB~QHBoxLayout\fR ()"
.br
.in -1c
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QHBoxLayout class lines up widgets horizontally.
.PP
This class provides an easier way to construct horizontal box layout objects. See QBoxLayout for more details.
.PP
The simplest ways to use this class are:
.PP
.nf
.br
     QBoxLayout * l = new QHBoxLayout( widget );
.br
     l->setAutoAdd( TRUE );
.br
     new QSomeWidget( widget );
.br
     new QSomeOtherWidget( widget );
.br
     new QAnotherWidget( widget );
.fi
.PP
or
.PP
.nf
.br
     QBoxLayout * l = new QHBoxLayout( widget );
.br
     l->addWidget( existingChildOfWidget );
.br
     l->addWidget( anotherChildOfWidget );
.fi
.PP
See also: QVBoxLayout, QGridLayout and Layout overview documentation
.PP
Examples:
.(l
layout/layout.cpp popup/popup.cpp
.)l
.SH MEMBER FUNCTION DOCUMENTATION
.SH "QHBoxLayout::QHBoxLayout ( QLayout * parentLayout, int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Creates a new horizontal box and adds it to \fIparentLayout.\fR
.SH "QHBoxLayout::QHBoxLayout ( QWidget * parent, int border=0, int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Creates a new top-level horizontal box.
.SH "QHBoxLayout::QHBoxLayout ( int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Creates a new horizontal box. You have to add it to another layout.
.SH "QHBoxLayout::~QHBoxLayout ()"
Destroys this box.
